{"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"Overview","text":"Overview","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"SQLite is thread-safe in the sense that the C library can be configured to serialize access internally, but using it correctly from Swift still requires discipline — prepared statements, transactions, and the connection state are all stateful and must not be touched from multiple threads concurrently."}]},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"LoomCore uses a ","type":"text"},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"single global actor"}]},{"text":" to serialize every ","type":"text"},{"code":"sqlite3_*","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" call:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["@globalActor","public actor DatabaseActor {","  public static let shared = DatabaseActor()","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Every public method on "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/Database"},{"text":", every static method on ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/Bindable"},{"text":", and every closure passed in (","type":"text"},{"code":"Binder","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"Stepper","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"transaction","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"‘s body) is ","type":"text"},{"code":"@DatabaseActor","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"-isolated. Swift’s compiler enforces this at the call site — you cannot call into LoomCore from arbitrary async code without first hopping to the actor.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","text":"What this guarantees","anchor":"What-this-guarantees","level":3},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"No two SQLite calls run at the same time, ever, in your process."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"No accidental shared mutable state between callers — the actor is the single point of synchronization.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Sendable"},{"text":" values you pass into binders and steppers are safe to capture; mutable references are flagged at compile time.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Once an operation starts executing, it runs to completion synchronously on the actor. Interleaving between tasks happens only at suspension points — never in the middle of a statement."}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"type":"heading","text":"The transaction gate","anchor":"The-transaction-gate","level":3},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Actor isolation alone is not enough for transactions: ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/DatabaseActor","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" releases its executor at every ","type":"text"},{"code":"await","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", so a transaction body that suspends would otherwise let another task’s statements run inside the open transaction. LoomCore closes that hole with a ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"gate","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"While a transaction is in flight — including while its body is suspended — database operations from tasks outside the transaction suspend at the gate and resume once the transaction commits or rolls back. Membership is a task-local token bound around the transaction block: structured children (","type":"text"},{"code":"async let","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", task groups) and unstructured ","type":"text"},{"code":"Task {}","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" inherit it and run inside the transaction — an unstructured task must complete before the body returns, or it races the commit; ","type":"text"},{"code":"Task.detached","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" does not inherit it and waits like any outside caller. An operation waiting at the gate throws ","type":"text"},{"code":"CancellationError","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" if its task is cancelled.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The gate is what makes ","type":"text"},{"code":"await","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" inside a transaction body safe. When no transaction is active it costs a single nil check. See ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/TransactionsAndServices","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" for the full semantics, including savepoint nesting.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","text":"Cancellation","anchor":"Cancellation","level":3},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Cancellation is ambient — no opt-in, no API knob:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Waiting at the gate"}]},{"text":" — a cancelled waiter resumes throwing ","type":"text"},{"code":"CancellationError","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", leaving the in-flight transaction undisturbed.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Mid-statement"}]},{"text":" — cancelling a task whose ","type":"text"},{"code":"exec","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"query","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", or ","type":"text"},{"code":"execScript","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is stepping aborts the statement via ","type":"text"},{"code":"sqlite3_interrupt","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (the one SQLite call that is safe cross-thread on a live connection) and throws ","type":"text"},{"code":"CancellationError","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". This works even inside a single long-running step, and a per-operation ticket guarantees a late-firing cancellation can never abort a different task’s statement.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"An interrupted ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"write","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" inside an explicit transaction makes SQLite roll the whole transaction back; ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/Database\/transaction(kind:_:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" recognizes that, reports a rollback to services, and leaves the connection open.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/Database\/interrupt()","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" exposes the same abort switch directly — it is ","type":"text"},{"code":"nonisolated","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", so any thread can stop a long query on a busy connection without cancelling the task running it. The interrupted operation throws ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/LoomError","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" with ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/SQLiteResultCode\/interrupt","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/Database\/directAccess(_:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" is the exception: it runs no LoomCore statements, so nothing is armed — code inside it manages its own cancellation.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","text":"What this rules out","anchor":"What-this-rules-out","level":3},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Concurrent reads against the same "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Database"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"text":" Even if SQLite would allow it (e.g. in WAL mode), LoomCore serializes everything through the actor. If you want true read parallelism, open multiple ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/Database"},{"text":" instances against the same file — each has its own connection and runs on its own actor turn.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Cross-actor "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"StatementHandle"},{"type":"text","text":" use."}]},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/StatementHandle"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/DatabaseHandle"},{"text":" are ","type":"text"},{"code":"~Copyable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and isolated to ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/DatabaseActor"},{"text":". They cannot escape into other contexts.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"type":"heading","text":"Resource cleanup","anchor":"Resource-cleanup","level":3},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/DatabaseHandle","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" owns the ","type":"text"},{"code":"sqlite3*","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" pointer plus the prepared-statement cache. It is ","type":"text"},{"code":"~Copyable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" to enforce single ownership. Cleanup happens in two ways:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"orderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Explicit close"}]},{"text":" — ","type":"text"},{"code":"db.close()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" finalizes cached statements and closes the connection eagerly.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"deinit"}]},{"text":" — the handle dispatches a ","type":"text"},{"code":"Task { @DatabaseActor … }","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" that runs the same cleanup. Because deinit can run on any thread, the cleanup work is moved into a ","type":"text"},{"code":"Task","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" whose body is on ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/DatabaseActor"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The cache is captured via a small reference-counted ","type":"text"},{"code":"ResourceStore","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" so it survives the move into the cleanup task. You should not normally see this internal structure — it just means resources are released safely without you having to think about it.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","text":"Working with SwiftUI and structured concurrency","anchor":"Working-with-SwiftUI-and-structured-concurrency","level":3},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"Database","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is ","type":"text"},{"code":"Sendable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", so it can be passed across actor boundaries. The methods that mutate it are isolated to ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/DatabaseActor","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":":","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["struct User: Sendable {","  let id: Int","  let name: String","}","","@MainActor","final class UserStore {","  let db: Database","","  init(db: Database) {","    self.db = db","  }","","  func loadUsers() async throws -> [User] {","    try await db.query(\"SELECT id, name FROM users\") { stmt, _ in","      User(","        id: try Int.column(of: stmt, at: 0),","        name: try String.column(of: stmt, at: 1)","      )","    }","  }","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The ","type":"text"},{"code":"await","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is the actor hop from ","type":"text"},{"code":"@MainActor","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" to ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/DatabaseActor","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":". Results returned to the main actor must be ","type":"text"},{"code":"Sendable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]}]}],"kind":"article","variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/loomcore\/concurrencymodel"]}],"sections":[],"abstract":[{"text":"How LoomCore makes SQLite race-free without explicit locking.","type":"text"}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/ConcurrencyModel"},"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"LoomCore"}],"roleHeading":"API Collection","role":"collectionGroup","title":"Concurrency and Actor Isolation"},"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore"]]},"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/Database","doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/DatabaseActor","doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/DatabaseHandle","doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/StatementHandle"],"anchor":"Topics"}],"seeAlsoSections":[{"title":"Articles","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/IndexConventions","doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/SafeInterpolation","doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/StoringCustomTypes","doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/QueryingJSON","doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/FullTextSearch","doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/TransactionsAndServices"],"anchor":"Articles"}],"references":{"doc://LoomCore/documentation/LoomCore/Database/transaction(kind:_:)":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"transaction"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"T"},{"kind":"text","text":">("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"kind"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:8LoomCore15TransactionKindO","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"TransactionKind"},{"kind":"text","text":", ("},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:8LoomCore8DatabaseC","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Database"},{"kind":"text","text":") "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"async"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"throws"},{"kind":"text","text":" -> "},{"text":"T","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"kind":"text","text":") "},{"text":"async","kind":"keyword"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"text":"throws","kind":"keyword"},{"kind":"text","text":" -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"T"}],"abstract":[{"text":"Runs a block of operations atomically inside a transaction.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/Database\/transaction(kind:_:)","title":"transaction(kind:_:)","type":"topic","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/loomcore\/database\/transaction(kind:_:)"},"doc://LoomCore/documentation/LoomCore/QueryingJSON":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Extract, filter, modify, build, and iterate JSON documents with typed expressions over SQLite’s JSON functions."}],"url":"\/documentation\/loomcore\/queryingjson","title":"Querying JSON","identifier":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/QueryingJSON","kind":"article","role":"collectionGroup"},"doc://LoomCore/documentation/LoomCore/SafeInterpolation":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"When "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"\\(value)"},{"type":"text","text":" becomes a parameter, when it becomes literal text, and how to keep injection-prone surfaces small."}],"url":"\/documentation\/loomcore\/safeinterpolation","title":"Safe SQL Interpolation","identifier":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/SafeInterpolation","kind":"article","role":"collectionGroup"},"doc://LoomCore/documentation/LoomCore":{"abs